the onyx logic metagenomics program will  be starting very soon  in this online program we will explore  the amazing role microbes play in the  environment  human health and disease designed to be  equally rewarding to students and  researchers the program will cover the  main aspects of microbiome studies  using next generation sequencing  overview of metagenomic sequencing  analysis of microbiome composition and  species richness  as well as other aspects of microbiology  research  using bioinformatics during this program  you will also  have the opportunity to apply  bioinformatics analysis methods  to research projects analyzing data  from the public domain and learning from  high impact biomedical publications  on relevant topics metagenomics is the  study of microbial communities in their  original living places  but many approaches to study these  communities allow for various levels of  resolution and  functional annotation so in this program  we will discuss  how the 16s ribosomal rna gene  amplicon studies hypervariable region  amplification  or even whole metagenomic sequencing and  even meta transcriptome studies  are revealing the significance of  microorganisms  all around us  to achieve this goal we constructed  a carefully designed program that  combines  interactive sessions self-guided study  materials that you can access  in a synchronous fashion as well as many  practical assignments  using both a visual interface and coding  practical assignments in the online  coursework  you will dive into the world of the  microbiome with this three-course series  introduction to metagenomics where you  will familiarize yourself  with the way microbiomes influence their  hosts and compose a unique community  which we can study using next-generation  sequencing  metagenomics one will focus on the  impact of bacterial diversity on human  health  where you will learn about multiple  types of sequencing methods  and then practice analysis using the  user-friendly t-binding for platform  and metagenomics 2 which builds on  previous courses to discuss 16s amplicon  sequencing studies  and the data2 analysis pipeline  specifically designed  for the analysis of these kinds of data  sets  in the course you will get a detailed  overview of  key topics important terminology  as well as a detailed and technical  overview  of the methods applied to these kinds of  data sets  the interactive tbionfor platform allows  you to process  analyze and integrate big data with no  coding  so we will learn how to apply some of  the tools on the platform  to study 16s microbial rna  you will find that on the interface of  the tibial  platform you can easily find the  relevant methods  with detailed explanations of what each  step of the method does  to allow us to study the microbiome  composition  and diversity we will also go further  and look at how we can use popular  methods of analysis  as well as visualization to understand  interpret  and visualize microbial community data  to learn about metagenomics we will  discuss what the microbiome is  how we can use next generation  sequencing to study  whole microbial communities and analyze  individual microbial genomes we will  also discuss  data sets or projects that are available  for analysis and study  of the role microbes play in agriculture  biomedical research topics and even  epidemiological studies  of infectious and chronic diseases  16s amplicon sequencing is a  recently developed and popular technique  that is widely used  to study micron directly in its  environment  so we will discuss how the bacterial 16s  ribosomal gene contains specific  hypervariable regions  that allow us to study different levels  of taxonomy  these levels of taxonomy are based on  annotated databases where we can find  metagenomic sequences  and link hypervariable regions to aid  in taxonomic classification so we will  apply this kind of analysis to a variety  of different projects for example  in the american gut project we will see  how the citizen science project  that is dedicated to metagenomic  sequencing of world citizens  who are contributing their microbiome  samples to allow researchers to  understand  microbiome variability and association  with particular traits  we will also look at some untrivial  relationship between the microbiome  the human immune system as well as the  anxiety  that is caused specifically by microbial  composition  then we will focus on individual members  of some of these microbial communities  that  are highly pathogenic cause chronic  conditions  or even affect different aspects of  crop production i welcome you to join  armex logic metagenomics we will have a  total of six  interactive sessions you will get  support from our trained  mentors and be able to participate  in group projects to analyze data sets  interpret them and develop a  presentation  based on what you have learned
 

